   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off Figure 1's side, plan and front views (tools/trace/crj7/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. The side view is drawn at the 1.8 degree static ground angle and was turned level. A T-tail (the tailplane on the fin's top fairing) with winglets and two CF34-8C nacelles on stub pylons on the rear fuselage. The side view draws the 20 cabin windows a side, the passenger door, the overwing exit (0.52 by 1.02 m drawn, Table 3's 0.51 by 0.97 m opening) and the forward and aft cargo doors, both on the left (Figure 4). The right side's service door is placed from Figure 4's dashed outline, relative to the passenger door. The aft cargo door's top is behind the nacelle in the drawing: its height is Table 3's 0.84 m. The engine's position is Detail A's: 59.6 in from the centerline to the nacelle's inner side and 61.1 in across, its middle 2.29 m out. All checks within 0.6%."
  }
